    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d311-a4">

                <pb facs="0632" n="508" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg508"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4 in No. 138.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Lord Granville to Mr. Lowell.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-02-25"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 25,
                        1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your communication of the 22d instant inclosing copies of the affidavits of
                    the masters of two United States fishing vessels detailing the acts of violence
                    by which they have been prevented from exercising their rights of fishing in
                    certain Newfoundland waters, and I have to state to you in reply that I have
                    forwarded copies to Her Majesty’s secretary of state for the colonies.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>GRANVILLE.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
